prompt:
Use Three.js to implement a Ferrari circuit racing game. Load the ToyCar.glb model as the player's race car and compete against an AI opponent in a 3-lap race on a circuit.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/ToyCar.glb as the player's race car;
(2) After loading, scale the model appropriately and place it at the track's starting point;
(3) After loading is complete, set window.__3D_STATE__.modelLoaded = true;

[Track Construction]
(4) Create a circuit track using TorusGeometry or a custom curve (radius 40 meters, track width 8 meters), with a dark gray asphalt material (0x333333);
(5) Place curbs with alternating red and white stripes along both sides of the track;
(6) Distribute 4 checkpoints evenly around the track, marked by translucent arches in different colors: yellow, blue, green, and purple. Make an arch flash when the player passes through its checkpoint;
(7) Mark the start/finish line with a black-and-white checkerboard pattern;
(8) Place grass planes inside and outside the track, and use 0x87CEEB for the sky background;

[AI Opponent]
(9) Create an AI opponent race car using a simple BoxGeometry box model colored red (0xff0000), and have it drive automatically along the track centerline;
(10) Set the AI speed to approximately 8-12 m/s, with small random fluctuations;
(11) Make the AI race car move smoothly along the track path and turn automatically;

[Driving Controls]
(12) Use the W key to accelerate, with a maximum speed of 15 m/s, and the S key to brake/reverse, with a minimum speed of -3 m/s;
(13) Use the A/D keys to steer left/right. Steering speed must depend on vehicle speed, with more responsive turning at low speeds;
(14) Natural deceleration: when W is not pressed, gradually reduce the speed using a friction decay factor of 0.98;
(15) The race car must drive along the track, and its speed must decrease when it reaches the track edge due to greater friction on the grass;
(16) Make the camera follow behind the race car from a third-person perspective with smooth following;

[Race Logic]
(17) The race consists of 3 laps. The player must pass through all 4 checkpoints in order for each lap to be valid;
(18) When passing a checkpoint, briefly display a HUD notification ("Checkpoint X/4");
(19) Display the lap time when a lap is completed;
(20) End the race after 3 laps and display the final position and total time;
(21) If the player is the first to complete 3 laps, display "You win!"; otherwise, display "AI wins!";

[HUD Display]
(22) Display the following in the upper-left HUD:
  - Current speed (id="speed", km/h)
  - Current lap (id="lap", format "1/3")
  - Checkpoint progress (id="checkpoints", format "2/4")
  - Race position (id="position", "1st" or "2nd")
  - Current lap time (id="lapTime", seconds, rounded to 1 decimal place)
  - Total time (id="totalTime", seconds, rounded to 1 decimal place)

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
{
  modelLoaded: boolean,
  speed: number,
  lap: number,
  totalLaps: number,
  checkpointsPassed: number,
  totalCheckpoints: number,
  position: number,
  lapTime: number,
  totalTime: number,
  raceState: string,
  aiLap: number,
  aiCheckpoints: number,
  playerAngle: number,
  aiAngle: number
}

Output a single HTML file in the same directory as the assets/ folder and run it through a local HTTP server.
